findings.suggestion:
Revert the `return err` line. Instead, escalate the log level to Warn when ErrDeviceLimitReached is returned, so the condition is observable without breaking anonymous user requests:

```go
err = a.tagDeviceUI(ctx, httpReq, taggedDevice)
if err != nil {
    if errors.Is(err, anonstore.ErrDeviceLimitReached) {
        a.log.Warn("Anonymous device limit reached, skipping device tag", "deviceID", deviceID, "error", err)
    } else {
        a.log.Debug("Failed to tag device for UI", "error", err)
    }
}
return nil
```

Remove the orphaned wire provider and bind from `wire.go`:
```go
// Remove these two lines from wireSet (wire.go ~line 374-375):
// anonstore.ProvideAnonDBStore,
// wire.Bind(new(anonstore.AnonStore), new(*anonstore.AnonDBStore)),
```
Since `ProvideAnonymousDeviceService` now constructs the store internally from `db.DB`, wire no longer needs to know about `ProvideAnonDBStore` or the interface bind. This keeps the wire graph accurate and avoids a confusing diff on the next `wire generate`.
